        "original_id": "6bc877e9-0599-50b4-8213-dc7d9f5e53be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Walker, David Usher, Brian Robertson\n- Organizations: Suburban Legends, Moist, Bomb Squad\n- Products: Poisonous Candy Factory\n- Topics: third-wave ska, alternative rock, music roles\n\nFacts:\n- David Usher was born on April 24, 1966, and he is an English-born Canadian musician, best-selling author, keynote speaker, and activist.\n- Brian Robertson was born on October 19, 1979, and he is the trombone player for the Orange County-based third-wave ska band Suburban Legends.\n- Vincent Francis Walker was born on March 2, 1980, and he is an American multi-instrumentalist better known as Vince Walker.\n- David Usher is known as the lead singer of the alternative rock band Moist.\n- Vince Walker is best known as the lead singer of the third-wave ska band Suburban Legends.\n- Brian Robertson and Vincent Walker are the two members who have played with Suburban Legends since its origin as Bomb Squad.\n- Poisonous Candy Factory is the second DVD released by the third wave ska/funk/pop band Suburban Legends.",
